Hours Worked: 10.5 hours

Logbook Entry:

Developed Section 36 of the MW–M31 merger analysis pipeline, introducing a comprehensive framework for characterizing halo morphology using complementary angular and topological diagnostics. Designed and implemented a spherical harmonic multipole expansion module to quantify the angular structure of the dark matter halo through radial shell decomposition, computing multipole coefficients, normalized power spectra, quadrupole and dipole strengths, phase information, and inner–outer isophote twist measurements. Constructed radial multipole profiles across multiple simulation snapshots to monitor the temporal evolution of large-scale asymmetries and non-axisymmetric structure throughout the merger.

Implemented a three-dimensional Minkowski functional analysis pipeline by generating Cloud-In-Cell density grids, applying Gaussian smoothing, and evaluating excursion sets across a range of density thresholds. Computed the complete set of Minkowski functionals (W0–W3), Euler characteristic, shapefinders, planarity, filamentarity, connected-component statistics, and topology-change diagnostics to quantify the evolving geometric and topological properties of the halo.

Developed routines to summarize morphological evolution through time-series diagnostics, including filamentarity, planarity, Euler characteristic evolution, topology transition counts, and morphology-plane trajectories. Established cross-method comparisons between multipole-based shape measures and tensor-derived ellipticity proxies, calculated Pearson correlation statistics between independent diagnostics, and implemented an automated morphology classification scheme to identify spherical, prolate, oblate, triaxial, and complex merger states.

Generated a comprehensive suite of scientific visualizations, including multipole power spectra, radial heatmaps, full multipole spectrum maps, quadrupole phase evolution, Minkowski functional curves, morphology-plane diagrams, Euler characteristic heatmaps, cross-diagnostic comparison plots, normalized evolutionary time-series, and a master summary panel consolidating all major diagnostics. Built an animation illustrating the coupled evolution of multipole spectra, morphology-plane trajectories, and global structural metrics throughout the merger simulation. Performed validation of the complete analysis workflow, verified numerical consistency across diagnostics, organized output generation, and documented the methodology for integration into the broader six-method morphological analysis framework.
